==== Looping ====
Jukeboxes disable adjacent hoppers while a music disc is playing inside them, due to them emitting a redstone signal even without using a comparator. When the song ends, the hopper placed below the jukebox is re-enabled, so the disc is automatically pulled out and stored in the hopper. To pull out the disc before the song ends, a [[minecart with hopper]] can be used, since it is not affected by the jukebox's redstone impulse.

A system of hoppers and droppers can then be used to automatically re-insert the disc, causing it to loop. Multiple different discs can be inserted into a system to create music playlists.

If a hopper under the jukebox is powered by anything else, it does not eject the disc, allowing systems to be paused once the current disc stops playing.

==== Playlists ====
{{in development|drop=Fourth Drop 2026|section=1}}
A [[chest]], [[trapped chest]], or any variant of [[copper chest]] that is a single block (not a large/“double” chest) can be placed on top of a jukebox and allow it to cycle through music discs in a queue as a playlist. 

An empty jukebox takes and plays a music disc from the first available slot in the chest above it, skipping empty slots and non-music-disc items. When the music disc is finished playing, it is inserted back into the chest and the next available one is taken. Manually ejecting a music disc that is currently playing will cause the next disc in the queue to immediately start playing. Additionally, the music disc in the chest that is the next to play displays the message "Playing Next" in its tooltip.

=== Fuel ===
Jukeboxes can be used as a [[fuel]] in [[furnace]]s, smelting 1.5 items per block.

=== Piston interactivity ===
Jukeboxes cannot be pushed by [[piston]]s. They also cannot be pushed or pulled by [[sticky piston]]s.

