A '''jack o'lantern''' is a variant of [[pumpkin]] that emits [[light]], and can be used to build [[golems]].

== Obtaining ==
=== Breaking ===
Jack o'lanterns are best mined with an [[axe]].
{{breaking row|horizontal=1|Jack o'Lantern|Axe|sword=1}}

=== Natural generation ===
Jack o'lanterns can spawn within [[taiga]] [[village]]s in [[pile]]s of pumpkins that also generate there.

=== Crafting ===
{{Crafting
|B2= Carved Pumpkin
|B3= Torch
|Output=Jack o'Lantern
|type= Building block
}}

== Usage ==
=== Light ===
[[File:Underwater Jack o'Lanterns.png|thumb|Jack o'lanterns can be used as light sources underwater.]]
A jack o'lantern emits more [[light]] than the [[torch]] used to craft it, being the highest level of 15. They also provide light while submerged under [[water]]. Like most light sources, they melt [[snow]] and [[ice]]. With the "Render Dragon Features for Creators" [[experiment]], jack o'lanterns have a [[light color]] of {{color|#d3852b}}.

Unlike most other blocks that emit light level 15, jack o'lanterns are a valid block to spawn on for mobs that ignore light level.

=== Building golems ===
{| style="float:right"
| [[File:Snow Golem.png|thumb|128px|Snow golem]]
| [[File:Iron Golem.png|thumb|128px|Iron golem]]
| [[File:Copper Golem.png|thumb|128px|Copper golem]]
|}
Jack o'lanterns can be used to build [[snow golem]]s,  [[iron golem]]s, and [[copper golem]]s as shown below. Snow golems require 2 [[snow block]]s for their bodies, iron golems require 4 [[iron block]]s, and copper golems require 1 [[copper block]]. The jack o'lantern must be placed last or the golem cannot spawn.

{{FakeImage|align=none|style=display:inline-block;margin:0|{{BlockGrid|scale=2|p=Jack o'Lantern|s=Snow Block| p | s | s }}|Snow golem build configuration}}
{{FakeImage|align=none|style=display:inline-block;margin:0|{{BlockGrid|scale=2|p=Jack o'Lantern|i=Block of Iron| p |iii| i }}|Iron golem build configuration}}
{{FakeImage|align=none|style=display:inline-block;margin:0|{{BlockGrid|scale=2|p=Jack o'Lantern|s=Block of Copper| p | s }}|Copper golem build configuration}}

=== Placement ===
Jack o'lanterns can be placed without a block under them. When placed, jack o'lanterns automatically face the [[player]]. Jack o'lanterns can be placed on a transparent block. However, {{in|Java}} the stems are directional, meaning the stem will point towards the face, while {{in|Bedrock}} the stems are non-directional, meaning the stems always face northwest just like normal [[pumpkin]]s.

Jack o'lanterns are transparent in their rendering only; otherwise, they share the attributes of all opaque solid blocks. For example, mobs can spawn on them, they can suffocate mobs, and blocks attached to another block (such as torches and rails) can be placed on top of them or on their sides.

Unlike a carved pumpkin, a jack o'lantern cannot be [[Armor|worn]].

=== Piston interactivity ===
Jack o'lanterns are destroyed when pushed by [[piston]]s, and cannot be pulled by [[sticky piston]]s.

