{{main|Pressure Plate#Usage}}

==== Activation ====
{{main|Pressure Plate#Activation}}

Heavy weighted pressure plates can be activated by most entities (including players, mobs, items, arrows, experience orbs, fishing bobs, etc.) and emit a redstone [[signal strength]] that is equal to {{frac|1|10}}  of the amount of entities on top of them (rounded up to the nearest integer), up to a maximum power level of 15. Certain entities, however (such as [[players]] in [[spectator mode]] and [[marker]]s), cannot activate them nor keep them activated.

{{IN|JE}}, [[item frame]]s and [[glow item frame]]s cannot activate heavy weighted pressure plates but they can still keep them activated.<ref>This behavior can be observed by placing an item frame inside of a heavy weighted pressure plate and then stepping on it: the pressure plate doesn't revert to its inactive state even after the player steps off.</ref>

The signal strength from a heavy weighted pressure plate does not vary with the type of entity. 15 mobs will produce the same signal strength as 15 different items. Note the heavy weighted pressure plate counts entities, not the quantity of items, generally leading to one entity count per stack of items. For more information see [[Item (entity)#Behavior| item entity behavior]].

